    <h1 id="contact-heading">Contact Mitch Chadban</h1>

    <h2>
Tell me what you are trying to fix, and you will get a straight answer on scope, timing and whether I am the right person for it.
    </h2>

    <p>
I am a freelance designer and marketer working with brands, SaaS companies and service businesses. Enquiries usually land in one of four areas, and most projects combine two or three of them.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>SEO</strong> — technical clean-ups, site structure, keyword and content strategy, and reporting that shows what actually moved.</li>
      <li><strong>AEO</strong> — earning citations in AI Overviews, ChatGPT and Perplexity, instead of hoping they pick you up on their own.</li>
      <li><strong>Design</strong> — brand systems, logos, illustration, landing pages and the templates that keep everything consistent afterwards.</li>
      <li><strong>Marketing</strong> — positioning, messaging, funnels and campaigns that turn attention into enquiries.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Who this work suits</h3>

    <ul>
      <li>SaaS and software companies that need organic search to become a reliable channel rather than a lucky quarter.</li>
      <li>Service businesses selling expertise — consultants, accountants, engineers, architects, advisers.</li>
      <li>Brands that look generic next to their competitors and already know it.</li>
      <li>Teams with an in-house marketer who need a specialist alongside them, not a replacement.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
It is a poor fit if you need rankings inside a fortnight, a full identity turned around for a couple of hundred dollars, or someone to publish AI-written content at volume. I will tell you that up front rather than take the brief.
    </p>

    <h3>What to include in your enquiry</h3>

    <p>
The more of this you cover in the first email, the sooner I can give you a real answer instead of booking a discovery call to find it out.
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li><strong>Your website</strong>, plus the specific pages that are underperforming if you already know which ones they are.</li>
      <li><strong>What you want to achieve</strong> — more qualified leads, a rebrand, visibility in AI answers, a specific launch.</li>
      <li><strong>What you have already tried</strong>, including the things that did not work.</li>
      <li><strong>Your timeline</strong> — a launch date, a target quarter, or “no fixed deadline” are all useful answers.</li>
      <li><strong>A budget range</strong>, even a rough one. It saves us both a round of guessing.</li>
      <li><strong>Who is involved</strong> — who approves the work, and who I will deal with day to day.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Availability across AEST, CET and GMT</h3>

    <p>
I am based in Australia and available for remote projects across Australian, European and UK time zones. Meeting times are arranged around the project and confirmed when we book.
    </p>

    <h3>Send an enquiry</h3>

    <p>
There is no form here on purpose. Email goes straight to me, keeps your attachments and links intact, and gives you a record of what was said.
    </p>

